<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  CBR006 Structure Detail Report, ported from legacy's JasperServer report
  (cbr-legacy jasper-server .../CBR006_StructureDetailReport.rpt_jrxml), layout unchanged but for
  two faults it had:
  - Crossing Name, Forest Service Road / Project Name, Culvert Material, Superstructure, Deck Type,
    Abutments and Curb Type were one fixed line and cut off a longer value - a comment that stands
    in for the code can run to 2000 characters. Each sits in a row of its own now, a band whose
    dividers stretch with it, so the value wraps and the rows below move down.
  - Culvert Number printed with two decimals, "1.00"; it is a whole number.

  As in STRUCTURE_INVENTORY_DETAILED, the port fills from rows rather than SQL - legacy called
  CBR_STRCTRE_DTL_RPT - every field already formatted as legacy's patterns printed it. The ministry
  line (the CBR_HEADER subreport) is P_MINISTRY, the logo comes from the classpath through P_LOGO,
  and Date Printed is P_DATE_PRINTED, in Pacific time. A structure with more than one bridge or
  culvert record is one row per pair, and so prints in full once for each, as legacy's join did.
-->
